# $repo_name

This repository exists for one purpose: feedback about your Second Brain
Accelerator — the AI system delaware set up for you and your assistant.

## What lands here

- **Feedback reports** — something that broke, confused you, or an idea for
  something better — opened by `/report-feedback`, always after showing you
  the exact text and asking first.
- **Health reports** — periodic, content-free status snapshots (plugin and
  structure versions, sync health, counts) — opened by `/health-check` when
  you choose to share one.

Every issue opened here goes through a deterministic scrub check before it
is sent. It contains zero personal or business content: no note text, no
names of people or organizations, no meeting titles. The only identifying
fact is which deployment it came from, which is what makes it actionable.
Nothing is ever sent without your explicit approval — the skill shows you
the exact text first.

## What you see

This repository is yours. It is the only place your reports go: feedback
from other delaware clients is never visible here, and nothing you write
here is visible to them.

## What delaware does with issues opened here

delaware's product team triages each issue using the labels below, and
folds anything accepted back into the product for every deployment, not
only yours. Closing an issue here never removes it from delaware's own
record of your engagement.

| Label | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `feedback` | A report opened by `/report-feedback` |
| `health-report` | A status snapshot opened by `/health-check` |
| `triage:new` | Not yet reviewed |
| `triage:accepted` | Confirmed, going into the product |
| `triage:productized` | Shipped in a plugin release |
| `triage:declined` | Reviewed, not going forward, with a reason on the issue |
